LLAMA-3 PROMPT DEBUG
input_only: False
instruction: 'Create a guide for making homemade facial cleanser.'
target: 'Homemade facial cleansers can be a great way to ensure you’re using natural ingredients on your skin, without the harsh chemicals that can be found in store-bought products. Here’s a step-by-step guide on how to create your very own homemade facial cleanser:\n\nMaterials:\n- A container for your cleanser (preferably glass)\n- A small funnel (optional)\n- Measuring spoons\n- Mixing bowl\n- Whisk (or fork)\n- Ingredients\n- Essential oils (optional)\n\nIngredients:\n- 2 tablespoons of Raw Honey\n- 1 tablespoon of Baking Soda\n- 1/4 cup of Distilled Water \n- Few drops of Essential Oil (Tea tree or Lavender work best)\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Select a container for your cleanser. It’s important to choose a container that is airtight and that will keep your mixture fresh.\n\n2. Measure and gather all your ingredients. The combination of raw honey, baking soda, and distilled water will gently cleanse your skin, while the essential oil will add a wonderful scent and can help with acne-fighting properties.\n\n3. In a mixing bowl, use a whisk (or fork) and mix the raw honey and baking soda together until you obtain a consistent texture. \n4. Add your distilled water into the mixture slowly, while mixing with the whisk. If you’d like to adjust the consistency of your cleanser, you can add more or less water depending on your preference.\n\n5. For a gentle scent, add a few drops of essential oil. Tea tree and lavender are great options for all skin types, with tea tree having natural acne-fighting properties and lavender being soothing.\n\n6. Once you have achieved the desired texture and scent, carefully pour or transfer your cleanser mixture to your container.\n\n7. Store your homemade facial cleanser in a cool, dry place, and make sure to shake well before each use.\n\nAnd that’s it! You now have a homemade facial cleanser that is gentle on your skin and free of harsh chemicals. Enjoy!'
formatted_prompt: "<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nCreate a guide for making homemade facial cleanser.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nHomemade facial cleansers can be a great way to ensure you’re using natural ingredients on your skin, without the harsh chemicals that can be found in store-bought products. Here’s a step-by-step guide on how to create your very own homemade facial cleanser:\n\nMaterials:\n- A container for your cleanser (preferably glass)\n- A small funnel (optional)\n- Measuring spoons\n- Mixing bowl\n- Whisk (or fork)\n- Ingredients\n- Essential oils (optional)\n\nIngredients:\n- 2 tablespoons of Raw Honey\n- 1 tablespoon of Baking Soda\n- 1/4 cup of Distilled Water \n- Few drops of Essential Oil (Tea tree or Lavender work best)\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Select a container for your cleanser. It’s important to choose a container that is airtight and that will keep your mixture fresh.\n\n2. Measure and gather all your ingredients. The combination of raw honey, baking soda, and distilled water will gently cleanse your skin, while the essential oil will add a wonderful scent and can help with acne-fighting properties.\n\n3. In a mixing bowl, use a whisk (or fork) and mix the raw honey and baking soda together until you obtain a consistent texture. \n4. Add your distilled water into the mixture slowly, while mixing with the whisk. If you’d like to adjust the consistency of your cleanser, you can add more or less water depending on your preference.\n\n5. For a gentle scent, add a few drops of essential oil. Tea tree and lavender are great options for all skin types, with tea tree having natural acne-fighting properties and lavender being soothing.\n\n6. Once you have achieved the desired texture and scent, carefully pour or transfer your cleanser mixture to your container.\n\n7. Store your homemade facial cleanser in a cool, dry place, and make sure to shake well before each use.\n\nAnd that’s it! You now have a homemade facial cleanser that is gentle on your skin and free of harsh chemicals. Enjoy!<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nThis homemade facial cleanser recipe sounds great! Can you give me some suggestions on how to customize it for my specific skin type?<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nOf course, here are some suggestions for how you can tweak the recipe to better suit your skin type:\n\n1. For oily skin: Add 1-2 teaspoons of lemon juice or apple cider vinegar to help balance the skin's natural oils.\n\n2. For dry skin: Add 1-2 teaspoons of avocado oil or sweet almond oil to the mixture to help moisturize and nourish the skin.\n\n3. For sensitive skin: Remove the baking soda from the recipe and substitute it with finely ground oatmeal or rice flour, which are gentler on the skin.\n\n4. For acne-prone skin: Remove the baking soda from the recipe and add a few drops of tea tree oil, which has natural antibacterial properties that can help fight acne.\n\nRemember, it’s important to patch test any new formulation or ingredient to check if it suits your skin well. Apply a bit of the cleanser on your forearm and wait for 24 hours to see if you have any reaction. If you do, discontinue use immediately."
