input_only: False
instruction: 'Create a 10-slide PowerPoint presentation on the use of tidal power in the energy industry. Include information on the history of tidal power, the benefits and drawbacks of using tidal power, current global usage and future growth projections, and case studies of successful tidal power projects. Use a professional and clean design with easy-to-read fonts and minimal text on each slide. Include relevant images and graphs to support your content. Finally, provide a list of credible sources used in your research on a final reference slide.'
target: "I don't have the capability to create visual presentations. However, I can assist you in creating a well-balanced slide and provide you with content suggestions on each slide.\n\nslide 1: title slide\n- use a professional looking background\n- add a professional-looking title using bold fonts (make it simple and straightforward)\n\nslide 2: introduction\n- brief the audience about the subject matter\n- add an attractive image related to the topic \n\nslide 3: history of tidal power (description)\n- explain how tidal power has been used down through time and give some insights into the evolution of technology \n- add an image related to the history of tidal power.\n\nslide 4: advantages of tidal power\n- explain the benefits of using tidal power\n- add facts and figures in bullet points along with relevant images\n\nslide 5: environmental benefits\n- explain the environment and economic advantages of using tidal power at the global and local levels\n- provide relevant case studies to back up your claims\n\nslide 6: drawbacks of tidal power\n- describe the drawbacks of tidal power in detail\n- provide relevant statistics and images to back your claims\n\nslide 7: tidal power potential and growth\n- describe the tidal power potential in the context of global energy demands\n- provide statistics on projected future growth of tidal power usage\n\nslide 8: promising tidal power projects\n- detail some recent successful tidal power projects and their locations \n- discuss how they have enhanced local power generation\n- provide relevant images that add to the presentation\n\nslide 9: global tidal power usage\n- provide statistical figures of current tidal power capacity and its position in the global energy mix\n- provide tables or graphs to support your claims\n\nslide 10: concluding points/references\n- provide a conclusion summarizing the main points of your presentation\n- add credits and references used in your presentation\n\nremember, the key to delivering a great presentation is to create a professional look and feel with minimalistic designs, visuals, and text. Your audience should be able to understand the presentation's main points clearly without struggling with visual details."
formatted_prompt: "<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nCreate a 10-slide PowerPoint presentation on the use of tidal power in the energy industry. Include information on the history of tidal power, the benefits and drawbacks of using tidal power, current global usage and future growth projections, and case studies of successful tidal power projects. Use a professional and clean design with easy-to-read fonts and minimal text on each slide. Include relevant images and graphs to support your content. Finally, provide a list of credible sources used in your research on a final reference slide.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nI don't have the capability to create visual presentations. However, I can assist you in creating a well-balanced slide and provide you with content suggestions on each slide.\n\nslide 1: title slide\n- use a professional looking background\n- add a professional-looking title using bold fonts (make it simple and straightforward)\n\nslide 2: introduction\n- brief the audience about the subject matter\n- add an attractive image related to the topic \n\nslide 3: history of tidal power (description)\n- explain how tidal power has been used down through time and give some insights into the evolution of technology \n- add an image related to the history of tidal power.\n\nslide 4: advantages of tidal power\n- explain the benefits of using tidal power\n- add facts and figures in bullet points along with relevant images\n\nslide 5: environmental benefits\n- explain the environment and economic advantages of using tidal power at the global and local levels\n- provide relevant case studies to back up your claims\n\nslide 6: drawbacks of tidal power\n- describe the drawbacks of tidal power in detail\n- provide relevant statistics and images to back your claims\n\nslide 7: tidal power potential and growth\n- describe the tidal power potential in the context of global energy demands\n- provide statistics on projected future growth of tidal power usage\n\nslide 8: promising tidal power projects\n- detail some recent successful tidal power projects and their locations \n- discuss how they have enhanced local power generation\n- provide relevant images that add to the presentation\n\nslide 9: global tidal power usage\n- provide statistical figures of current tidal power capacity and its position in the global energy mix\n- provide tables or graphs to support your claims\n\nslide 10: concluding points/references\n- provide a conclusion summarizing the main points of your presentation\n- add credits and references used in your presentation\n\nremember, the key to delivering a great presentation is to create a professional look and feel with minimalistic designs, visuals, and text. Your audience should be able to understand the presentation's main points clearly without struggling with visual details.<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nI think it's a good start, but I would like to add more information on the drawbacks of using tidal power. Can you provide me with some more data and facts to include in slide 6?<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nCertainly! Here are some additional drawbacks of using tidal power to include in slide 6:\n\n- High capital costs: The initial investment in building tidal power plants can be expensive. - Maintenance costs: Maintenance costs for tidal power plants are also high due to the harsh marine environment they operate in. - Limited geographical availability: Tidal power plants require specific geographical features such as a large tidal range, which limits their availability to certain areas. - Impact on marine life: Tidal power plants can impact marine life, especially fish, mammals, and birds, as the turbines can injure or kill them. - Lack of predictability: The ability to generate electricity from tidal power is dependent on the predictable movement of tides. However, unexpected changes in tides or weather conditions can impact the plant's power generation. - Disruption of habitats: The construction of tidal power plants can disrupt habitats, including disrupting or destroying important breeding grounds for fish and other marine life. These are just a few examples of the drawbacks of using tidal power. With more research, you may be able to find additional points to add to your presentation."
